---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern your use of TinyTools calculators. The tools are provided free, as-is, for general information — not financial, tax, payroll, or legal advice."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="container prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Terms of Use" }]} />
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-08-31">31 August 2026</time></p>

    <p>
      By using <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a> ("the site") you agree to these
      terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} provides free online calculators for work hours, overtime, pay,
      and paycheck estimates. The tools are for general informational and
      educational use.
    </p>

    <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site is financial, tax, accounting, payroll, employment, or
      legal advice, and no professional relationship is created by using it.
      Results are estimates based on the inputs you provide and on published
      rates and formulas that can change or be applied differently in your
      situation. Overtime rules, tax withholding, and pay entitlements depend on
      your jurisdiction, employment classification, and individual circumstances.
      Always confirm important figures with your employer, payroll provider, a
      qualified professional, or the relevant government authority before relying
      on them.
    </p>

    <h2>No affiliation</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an independent site. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
      or connected to the IRS, HM Revenue &amp; Customs, the Canada Revenue
      Agency, the Australian Taxation Office, any state or provincial revenue
      body, or any employer or payroll company.
    </p>

    <h2>Provided "as is"</h2>
    <p>
      The site and its calculators are provided "as is" and "as available",
      without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including accuracy,
      fitness for a particular purpose, or uninterrupted availability. To the
      fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any loss or
      damage arising from use of, or reliance on, the site or its results.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the calculators for personal or business purposes. You may not
      attempt to disrupt the site, scrape it at a scale that degrades service for
      others, misrepresent it as your own, or use it for unlawful purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The {SITE.name} name, design, written content, and calculator
      implementations are our property or used with permission. Published tax
      rates, statutes, and government formulas referenced by the tools are not
      our property.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The site is supported by advertising. Ads are labelled and kept separate
      from calculator controls and results. We are not responsible for the
      content of third-party ads or the sites they link to.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms or the calculators at any time. Continued use
      after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: see the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
